{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Exp","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L228-L238","doc":"The Borromean Markov trace has zero bar-anti-symmetric companion over `ℝ`\n(named alias of `Q_borromean_real_eq_zero`, kept resolvable for downstream\nconsumers that referred to `Q_borromean_eq_zero` by name; see also the `ℚ`\nversion `QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean_eq_zero` in\n`BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean`).\n\nPreviously a `def Q_borromean_eq_zero : True := trivial` placeholder shim;\nde-vacuified to carry the real statement now that `Q_borromean_real_eq_zero`\nproves it (AGENTS.md §1a — no `: True` dodges). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_real_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_real_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L200-L226","doc":"**The Borromean Markov trace has zero bar-anti-symmetric companion,\nover `ℝ`.**\n\nThe closed form `(4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶) / (h² + 4)` has all-even-power\nnumerator and denominator, so `trM_borromean_real (−h) = trM_borromean_real h`\nby `ring`. The bar-anti-symmetric projection\n`Q_borromean_real h := (trM(h) − trM(−h)) / 2` therefore vanishes\nidentically.\n\nThis is the **ℝ-side lift** of the `ℚ` proof in\n[`QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Q_borromean_eq_zero`](../BraidsAndKnots/BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean)\n(PR #1211, commit `5329eb054`).  No `Rat.cast` lift is needed —\nthe `ring` proof works uniformly over any `CommRing` of\ncharacteristic 0; the `noncomputable` qualifier is purely because\nof `(_ : ℝ) / (_ : ℝ)` division, not because of any irrational input.\n\nHistory:\n  - `d4d640ce7` (sibling): placeholder `True := trivial`\n  - PR #1196: documented the gap in [`docs/audits/2026-05-24-sinh-\n    cosh-lean-integration-audit.md`](../../../../../docs/audits/2026-05-24-sinh-cosh-lean-integration-audit.md)\n  - PR #1211: full proof over `ℚ` in `BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean`\n    (commit `5329eb054`)\n  - this PR (item E): **ℝ-side lift here**, with `Q_borromean_real`\n    def + theorem proven via `ring` (uniform with the `ℚ` proof) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_borromean_real","kind":"def","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L195-L198","doc":"The bar-anti-symmetric companion of the Borromean Markov trace,\nover `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.trM_borromean_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.trM_borromean_real","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L190-L193","doc":"The Borromean Markov trace closed form over `ℝ`, parallel to the\n`ℚ` version in `BorromeanMarkovTrace.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L156-L173","doc":"The EM-channel ratios are monotonically increasing in m\n(since tanh is monotone increasing and (2m+1)·η_0 grows with m). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio_pos","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L148-L154","doc":"The per-particle EM-channel ratio is positive at substrate\n(since η_substrate > 0 and tanh is positive for positive input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.EM_channel_ratio","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L130-L139","doc":"The EM-channel ratio for particle T(2, 2m) at substrate.\n\nPer PR #1153 (merged commit 26e57945e): this equals\ntanh((2m+1)·η_substrate). Empirical values at substrate\n(50-dps mpmath, canonical pin):\n  W (m=2): 0.4790\n  Z (m=3): 0.6233\n  H (m=4): 0.7348 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.η_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.η_substrate","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L122-L128","doc":"The substrate-evaluation η₀ corresponding to q_0 ≈ 1.10998.\nDefined as log(q_0) where q_0 is the canonical 50-digit pin\n`qou_substrate.constants.Q_50_DIGIT_STR`\n(`1.10997859555418057528159407960950937799328227995870`,\nderived from CODATA m_μ/m_e + SnapPy Vol(4_1)).\nApproximately 0.10434. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.P_minus_Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.P_minus_Q","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L105-L111","doc":"The difference identity: $P_m - Q_m = e^{-(2m+1)\\eta} / (2 \\cosh η)$.\n\nProof: $\\cosh - \\sinh = e^{-x}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.P_plus_Q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.P_plus_Q","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L97-L103","doc":"The sum identity: $P_m + Q_m = e^{(2m+1)\\eta} / (2 \\cosh η)$.\n\nProof: $\\cosh + \\sinh = e^x$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_over_P_eq_tanh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_over_P_eq_tanh","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L84-L95","doc":"The tanh ratio identity:\n$Q_m / P_m = \\tanh((2m+1) \\eta)$.\n\nProof: trivial from sinh/cosh = tanh and the common $1/(2 \\cosh η)$\nfactors cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.pythagorean_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.pythagorean_identity","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L68-L82","doc":"The Pythagorean identity:\n$P_m^2 - Q_m^2 = 1/[2]_q^2$ (independent of m).\n\nThis is the KEY structural generalization from PR #1181 — all\ntorus knots T(2, 2m) satisfy the same Pythagorean constraint at\nsubstrate.\n\nProof: direct from cosh²(x) − sinh²(x) = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bracket_2_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bracket_2_q","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L65-L66","doc":"The quantum integer $[2]_q$ at substrate η: $[2]_q = q + q^{-1} = 2 \\cosh η$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Q_m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Q_m","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The bar-anti-symmetric Markov-trace component for T(2, 2m). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.P_m","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.P_m","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BarSymmetricBarAntiSymmetricIdentities.lean#L57-L59","doc":"The bar-symmetric Markov-trace component for T(2, 2m). ","signatureChunk":0}]}